## Phase

**Phase 2 — Tier B** (complete in product). **Deploy:** Alibaba ECS + Docker Compose — see `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` (live URL source of truth). Do not start Tier C.

Trigger: Tier B plan execution, deploy todos, or user names a Tier B/deploy todo.

## Deploy (cross-chat)

- Production: nginx same-origin `/api` + SQLite volume + durable HITL checkpoints.
- Before changing ports, CORS, API base URL, or DB path: read and update `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`.
- Do not assume localhost-only when adding features.

## Stack (locked)

| Layer | Choice | Do NOT use |
|-------|--------|------------|
| Orchestration | **LangGraph** (governed graph + HITL interrupt) | Hermes gateway, CrewAI-only |
| LLM | Qwen via DashScope / Qoder | OpenAI-only stack |
| API | FastAPI | |
| DB | SQLite → Postgres-ready | |
| UI | **Next.js 14** App Router | |
| Tools | MCP-style functions in `backend/app/tools/` | |

**Why not Hermes:** Product needs deterministic NGO workflow + custom SaaS UI + supervisor gate — LangGraph fits; Hermes is autonomous gateway-centric.

## Tier discipline

### Tier A — ship first (all required before Tier B)

1. Agent trace visible in UI
2. HITL supervisor (approve/reject)
3. Duplicate + critical demo paths
4. Metrics dashboard
5. Urdu + English live
6. Qwen/DashScope wired
7. Audit log

### Tier B — only after Tier A E2E green

Light RAG/SOPs, role-based views, case timeline, richer Lahore seed, PDF export.

### Tier C — defer unless rubric demands

WhatsApp production, real Alkhidmat API, mobile apps, 10+ agents, billing, CNIC OCR.

## Non-negotiable graph rule

`Intake → Triage → Knowledge → Integrity → Matcher → Dispatch` — **never skip Integrity** on create.

HITL gate when `critical` priority or high integrity risk.

